lf","\u002Finternals\u002Fwolf","7.internals\u002F6.wolf",{"id":213,"title":30,"body":214,"description":538,"extension":539,"links":540,"meta":541,"navigation":542,"path":31,"seo":543,"stem":32,"__hash__":544},"docs_en\u002F2.install\u002F1.wolf-app.md",{"type":215,"value":216,"toc":528},"minimark",[217,235,240,257,260,348,351,354,386,390,393,411,415,427,433,437,444,448,456,462,466,507,514,518,524],[218,219,220,221,225,226,230,231,234],"p",{},"The Wolf App (",[222,223,224],"code",{},"dodock_wolf",") runs on a Frappe or Dokos site. That site becomes the ",[227,228,229],"strong",{},"central"," Wolf\nsite: agents push to it, rules run on it, and the Wolf UI is served from it at ",[222,232,233],{},"\u002Fwolf",".",[236,237,239],"h2",{"id":238},"requirements","Requirements",[241,242,243,247,254],"ul",{},[244,245,246],"li",{},"Frappe 15 or Dokos (Dodock 5). Tested on Dodock 5.18, MariaDB 10.6 and Postgres 16 and 17.",[244,248,249,250,253],{},"Node 20.19 or later on the bench, for ",[222,251,252],{},"bench build"," of the Wolf UI.",[244,255,256],{},"A scheduler running every minute (below).",[236,258,24],{"id":259},"install",[261,262,268],"pre",{"className":263,"code":264,"filename":265,"language":266,"meta":267,"style":267},"language-bash shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","cd ~\u002Ffrappe-bench\nbench get-app https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fbthuner\u002Fdodock-wolf\nbench --site wolf.example.com install-app dodock_wolf\nbench build --app dodock_wolf   # links the static assets and builds the Wolf UI (\u002Fwolf)\nbench set-config -g scheduler_tick_interval 60\n","bench","bash","",[222,269,270,283,295,312,330],{"__ignoreMap":267},[271,272,275,279],"span",{"class":273,"line":274},"line",1,[271,276,278],{"class":277},"s2Zo4","cd",[271,280,282],{"class":281},"sfazB"," ~\u002Ffrappe-bench\n",[271,284,286,289,292],{"class":273,"line":285},2,[271,287,265],{"class":288},"sBMFI",[271,290,291],{"class":281}," get-app",[271,293,294],{"class":281}," https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fbthuner\u002Fdodock-wolf\n",[271,296,298,300,303,306,309],{"class":273,"line":297},3,[271,299,265],{"class":288},[271,301,302],{"class":281}," --site",[271,304,305],{"class":281}," wolf.example.com",[271,307,308],{"class":281}," install-app",[271,310,311],{"class":281}," dodock_wolf\n",[271,313,315,317,320,323,326],{"class":273,"line":314},4,[271,316,265],{"class":288},[271,318,319],{"class":281}," build",[271,321,322],{"class":281}," --app",[271,324,325],{"class":281}," dodock_wolf",[271,327,329],{"class":328},"sHwdD","   # links the static assets and builds the Wolf UI (\u002Fwolf)\n",[271,331,333,335,338,341,344],{"class":273,"line":332},5,[271,334,265],{"class":288},[271,336,337],{"class":281}," set-config",[271,339,340],{"class":281}," -g",[271,342,343],{"class":281}," scheduler_tick_interval",[271,345,347],{"class":346},"sbssI"," 60\n",[218,349,350],{},"Then restart the scheduler process.",[218,352,353],{},"Installing creates:",[241,355,356,367,378],{},[244,357,358,359,362,363,366],{},"the roles ",[227,360,361],{},"Wolf Manager"," (sees and configures everything) and ",[227,364,365],{},"Wolf User"," (read-only);",[244,368,369,370,373,374,377],{},"a random ",[227,371,372],{},"registration token"," in ",[227,375,376],{},"Wolf Settings",", used by agents to register;",[244,379,380,381,385],{},"the ",[382,383,384],"a",{"href":97},"preset alert rules",", with no channels.",[236,387,389],{"id":388},"scheduler-pace","Scheduler pace",[218,391,392],{},"Wolf's alert rules, rollups and satellite pushes are scheduled every minute. Frappe 15 and Dodock\ntick every 4 minutes by default.",[394,395,396],"warning",{},[218,397,398,399,402,403,406,407,410],{},"Without ",[222,400,401],{},"scheduler_tick_interval"," set to ",[222,404,405],{},"60",", an alert can come up to 4 minutes late, and \"fire\nafter 3 evaluations\" means 12 minutes. The Wolf UI's ",[227,408,409],{},"Monitoring"," page shows the pace in use.",[236,412,414],{"id":413},"the-wolf-ui","The Wolf UI",[218,416,417,420,421,423,424,426],{},[222,418,419],{},"https:\u002F\u002F\u003Csite>\u002Fwolf"," is the operator UI, a Vue app built on frappe-ui. It reuses the Frappe\nsession: guests go to the login page, users without ",[227,422,365],{}," or ",[227,425,361],{}," get a 403.\nDesk keeps the configuration DocTypes; a view the Wolf UI does not have yet links to Desk.",[428,429],"screenshot",{"alt":430,"caption":431,"name":432},"An incident in the Wolf UI","An incident: timeline, deployment marker, and the events grouped under it.","incident",[236,434,436],{"id":435},"language","Language",[218,438,439,440,443],{},"Desk and the Wolf UI show Wolf in each user's language (",[227,441,442],{},"My Settings → Language","). English and\nFrench are available: field labels, descriptions, buttons, messages, the Wolf UI's pages and the\nrule sentence. DocType names, event types, metric names and Select values stay in English, as in\nthe code. What Wolf stored when it happened stays in the language it was written in: incident\ntitles, event summaries, comments and the journal. Notifications and the SIEM export are in\nEnglish for now.",[236,445,447],{"id":446},"signals-with-no-agent","Signals with no agent",[218,449,450,451,453,454,234],{},"The Wolf site watches itself as soon as the app is installed: failed Scheduled Job Logs, Error Logs\nand failed backups, failed desk logins, privileged logins from a new IP or country, role grants,\nEmail Queue backlogs and risky application changes. Each can be turned off in ",[227,452,376],{},".\nSee ",[382,455,119],{"href":120},[218,457,458,459,234],{},"To get the same signals from the bench's other sites, install the app there too, as\n",[382,460,461],{"href":41},"satellites",[236,463,465],{"id":464},"upgrade","Upgrade",[261,467,469],{"className":263,"code":468,"filename":265,"language":266,"meta":267,"style":267},"bench update --apps dodock_wolf   # or: cd apps\u002Fdodock_wolf && git pull\nbench --site wolf.example.com migrate\nbench build --app dodock_wolf\n",[222,470,471,486,497],{"__ignoreMap":267},[271,472,473,475,478,481,483],{"class":273,"line":274},[271,474,265],{"class":288},[271,476,477],{"class":281}," update",[271,479,480],{"class":281}," --apps",[271,482,325],{"class":281},[271,484,485],{"class":328},"   # or: cd apps\u002Fdodock_wolf && git pull\n",[271,487,488,490,492,494],{"class":273,"line":285},[271,489,265],{"class":288},[271,491,302],{"class":281},[271,493,305],{"class":281},[271,495,496],{"class":281}," migrate\n",[271,498,499,501,503,505],{"class":273,"line":297},[271,500,265],{"class":288},[271,502,319],{"class":281},[271,504,322],{"class":281},[271,506,311],{"class":281},[218,508,509,510,513],{},"Migrations never overwrite presets you edited. A ",[222,511,512],{},"bench migrate"," is recorded as a deployment on\nthe Wolf timeline.",[236,515,517],{"id":516},"next","Next",[218,519,520,523],{},[382,521,522],{"href":36},"Install the agent"," on each host.",[525,526,527],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .s2Zo4, html code.shiki .s2Zo4{--shiki-light:#6182B8;--shiki-default:#82AAFF;--shiki-dark:#82AAFF}html pre.shiki code .sfazB, html code.shiki .sfazB{--shiki-light:#91B859;--shiki-default:#C3E88D;--shiki-dark:#C3E88D}html pre.shiki code .sBMFI, html code.shiki .sBMFI{--shiki-light:#E2931D;--shiki-default:#FFCB6B;--shiki-dark:#FFCB6B}html pre.shiki code .sHwdD, html code.shiki .sHwdD{--shiki-light:#90A4AE;--shiki-light-font-style:italic;--shiki-default:#546E7A;--shiki-default-font-style:italic;--shiki-dark:#676E95;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic}html pre.shiki code .sbssI, html code.shiki .sbssI{--shiki-light:#F76D47;--shiki-default:#F78C6C;--shiki-dark:#F78C6C}html .light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html.light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(-